    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="19">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Rect">Rect</ref> 19</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="19" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="452" ed="#liebermann"/>[19] Be wudewarde. Wuduwearde gebyreð ælc windfylled treow.</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="19" corresp="#wit-q"><pb n="452" ed="#liebermann"/>Ƿudeƿeard<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Rect_19.lnote.oe.1"/> (id est custodi nemoris uel forestario) iure cedit<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="2" target="#Rect_19.lnote.oe.2"/> lignum omne uento deiectum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="3" target="#Rect_19.lnote.oe.3"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#gobbitt" n="20" corresp="#wit-b">Be wudewarde . Wuduwearde gebyreð ælc wind fylled treow .</ab>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="ang" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="330" ed="#rabin-doml"/><hi rend="italic">Be wudewarde</hi> Wuduwearde gebyreð ælc windfylled treow.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="452" ed="#liebermann"/>Vom Waldwart<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Rect_19.lnote.de.1"/>. Dem Waldwart gebührt jeder vom Wind gefällte Baum.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">Of the woodward. To the woodward is due every tree blown down by the wind.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#gobbitt" corresp="#wit-b">Concerning the forester To the forester is due each wind-felled tree.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#rabin-doml" corresp="#wit-b"><pb n="331" ed="#rabin-doml"/><hi rend="italic">Regarding the Forester</hi> To the forester is due every tree felled by the wind.</ab>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rect_19.lnote.oe.1" n="1" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">452</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so T;</hi> -ward <hi rend="italic">übr.</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus T; -ward the others</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rect_19.lnote.oe.2" n="2" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">452</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">so TM;</hi> concedit <hi rend="italic">R;</hi> cecidit <hi rend="italic">Hk</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">thus TM; concedit R; cecidit Hk</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Rect_19.lnote.oe.3" n="3" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">452</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-cto <hi rend="italic">R</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-cto R</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Rect_19.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">252</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">1</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Vgl. Gl</hi> Wald 3; Windfall. Das Wort <hi rend="italic">wuduweard</hi> ging ins Mittelkymrische über; Windisch in <hi rend="italic">Abh. Sächs. Ges. Wiss</hi>. 29 VI (1912) 250.—In Battle ist der <hi rend="italic">wodeward</hi> zugleich Schweinehirt: <hi rend="italic">pro custodia porcorum habebit ad festum s. Martini intestina unius porci</hi>; Custumal of Battle ed. Scargill-Bird 67</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">Cf. <hi rend="italic">Gl</hi> Wald 3; Windfall. The word <hi rend="italic">wuduweard</hi> passed into Middle Welsh; Windisch in <hi rend="italic">Abh. Sächs. Ges. Wiss</hi>. 29 VI (1912) 250.—At Battle the <hi rend="italic">wodeward</hi> is at the same time swineherd: <hi rend="italic">pro custodia porcorum habebit ad festum s. Martini intestina unius porci</hi>; Custumal of Battle ed. Scargill-Bird 67</seg></note>
      </div>
